From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:12:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] kboot: admit the J604 per T8132 handoff path through
 t8132_board_admitted()

The J713 handoff paths ported from aurora-silicon/m1n1 #35-#48 each test
the root compatible against "apple,j713" (14 sites in dapf.c, kboot.c,
kboot_atc.c, kboot_gpu_m4.c, payload.c and pcie_fdt.c). Route them all
through one helper, t8132_board_admitted(fdt, path), backed by a
per-board table of admitted paths (src/t8132_board.h):

  J713: every path, exactly as before.
  J604: STORAGE, DISPLAY, GPU, DAPF, ATC_USB3, PCIE_RADIO. Not AOP.
  Any other board: no path, exactly as before.

Each J604 path is admitted only where the values it depends on match
the J713 in Apple's template device trees for Mac16,1 and Mac16,12 at
macOS 27.2 26B123 (the J604's system firmware) and 26.6.2 25G83 (the
stub). The SOURCE is  fetched
2026-11-04. Every value and its status is in docs/j604.md. Main points:

  - The register windows of dart-disp0/dart-dcp/dcp, sgx/gfx-asc
    (including the GPU interrupts 994/993/996/995), ans, dart-aop,
    dart-apcie0, apcie, dart-mtp/pmp/isp and pmgr are identical.
  - The radio rail matches: amfm function-reg_on is SMC gP13 pKW4
    0x00800000 on both boards, which is SMC_J713_RADIO_REG_ON_TEMPLATE.
  - CPU topology is identical (6 E + 4 P).

AOP is held back. On the J604, aop/iop-aop-nub aop-target is 0, while
on the J713 it is 1, and what it selects is not known. On the J604 the
AOP handoff therefore stays as on any unqualified M4 board
(dt_set_t8132_aop() returns early). The runtime values are TO-VERIFY on
the fresh 27.2 J604 capture: board-id,
memory and carveouts, DCP segments/UUID, GPU regions, and the AOP
segments. The admitted paths already validate their live ADT values
and refuse on a mismatch.

This replaces the earlier private draft's all-or-nothing admission
(aura 410aff89), whose evidence was a pre-reset live ADT. That evidence
is not used.

pcie_fdt.c comments now say that the J604 SD reader port
(pci-bridge2) shares the T8132 PCIe host and is disabled with the
radio after a failed handoff. docs/j604.md records the risk when the
kernel DT gives that port a pwren-gpios.

Tests:
  - New test_t8132_board_admission.py: J713 gets every path, J604 every
    path but AOP, and other or look-alike compatibles, a NULL tree or
    an out-of-range path get none. A mutant that admits the J604 AOP
    fails it.
  - test_m4_pcie_power_fdt.py also runs its power contract with a
    J604 tree.
  - test_j713_aop_dapf.py, test_j713_dapf_instance.py,
    test_m4_gpu_handoff.py, test_m4_pcie_power_fdt.py and
    test_smp_handoff_gate.py and test_m3_defaults_optout.py compile
    production text without its
    #include lines, so they now prepend src/t8132_board.h.
    test_smp_handoff_gate's fdt_node_check_compatible stub takes a
    const tree, like libfdt.

Build (RELEASE=1 CHAINLOADING=1, clang/lld 23.1.4): no new warnings.

Hardware tested on: NOT YET
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
